.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/prompts/codex-sol-c3s-diagnostic-arms.md:22:Also add an **offline attribution tool** `attribute_c3s_receipts.py` that reads the v1 unit receipts (read-only) and reports, per arm and pooled: counts of executed configuration types (BASE, unilateral, evacuation), number of users moved per decision, active-beam counts per step (if recoverable from actions + masks; otherwise say so), cumulative EE advantage vs BASE by step (to show whether gains are early, steady or concentrated at the end), and the FULL-vs-LITE divergence steps with nominal vs realised deltas at those steps. Output JSON + Markdown.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/gpt-qa-c3s.md:16:This distinction matters: S0-U already achieves **+1.523%**, compared with S0’s **+1.813%** (`04-S0-PROBE-RESULT.md`, opening results table). Much of the observed benefit requires no evacuation. A learned S3 predictor would be a separate learner experiment; simulator-trained S3 would not automatically remove model privilege.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:18:Hierarchical load-aware LEO RL has different endpoints. Zhao et al., Demand-Aware Beam Hopping and Power Allocation for Load Balancing in Digital Twin empowered LEO Satellite Networks (2024 author preprint), use a cloud/digital-twin layer for beam hopping and a satellite layer for power allocation. Global requests, resource use and queue backlogs are available; arrivals have TTL queues, and the link model assumes clear sky and compensated Doppler. Section V-C2 reports an 82.13 Mbps load gap, 75.95% below Greedy BH. The abstract gives a less-specific 72.5% figure; use the body’s explicitly identified comparison. This is load-balancing evidence, not pooled EE or savings from whole-beam evacuation. Zhao et al., §§III–V.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:19:There is direct quantitative LEO power-saving evidence, but its conditions matter. Fastenbauer et al., LEO Satellite Beam Hopping for Power Consumption Minimization at Different Elevation Angles (IEEE OJCOMS 6, 2025), report 3.23 kW versus 32.1 kW for greedy hopping versus full illumination at 90° elevation, with 19 beams and 25 users demanding 10 Mbit/s each: approximately 90% lower modeled power. Their accounting includes PA supply, RF/phase-shifter costs and always-on fixed consumption; MMSE precoding assumes perfect CSI. This is low-utilization temporal beam hopping, not measured spacecraft savings or atomic user evacuation. In a separate seven-beam timing case, greedy takes 14.2 ms versus 230 s exhaustive search, yet the target hopping cycle is 10 ms; the authors explicitly acknowledge further speed work is needed. Fastenbauer et al., Eq. 28, Figs. 15 and 18, §VI.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:23:06-E1-RESULT-RECORD.md reports realised-information pooled oracle gains of 1.992311% for U₁ (at most one changed user per anchor) and 2.222094% for J₁ (the fixed evacuation catalog). These are restricted finite-panel optima, not unrestricted joint or trajectory ceilings. S0-U already improves EE by 1.523026%, versus 1.812631% for S0; S0-J includes singleton origins under 01, §3. Thus, neither the entire gain nor the S0-J gain identifies uniquely multi-user evacuation. No verified source in this bounded review quantifies precisely C3-S-style whole-origin evacuation above frozen learned heads; that is an evidence gap, not proof of novelty.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:60:E1 has unilateral headroom; S0-U is positive; evacuation includes singletons; exact O1 exposes residual BASE error.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:68:Suggested related-work wording: “C3-S combines learned per-user proposals with centralized model-based configuration selection, following the broad learning-plus-optimization pattern exemplified by DROO and satellite beam-pattern optimization. Its action catalog explicitly includes single-user edits and whole-origin evacuations, and each candidate is evaluated as a complete physical configuration before atomic execution. The contribution concerns this interface and its evaluation under the stated energy accounting, rather than the general invention of hybrid learning and optimization.”
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:69:Suggested discussion wording: “Across the tested target families and frozen additive deployment rules, accurate or exact counterfactual signals did not consistently produce beneficial joint execution. This result concerns the tested credit-to-action interface and does not refute difference-reward policy gradients or establish an impossibility of decentralized coordination. On matched development anchors, nominal-model configuration selection increased realised pooled EE by 1.812631% with unchanged aggregate served fraction. These findings motivate the declared closed-loop evaluation; sustained benefit and unique attribution to beam evacuation remain unestablished.”
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-chatgpt-package-20260908/outside-round3/astra-c3s-docx.md:92:Research limits: this was a bounded primary-source review, not an exhaustive novelty search. Full texts were checked for the central claims about DROO, COMA, statistical CSI, fractional programming and Fastenbauer’s power/latency results; several other sources were available only through author manuscripts or institutional/indexed abstracts, as indicated. The supplied chronology is a derived index and E1’s raw tape is not included. Searches covered hybrid selectors, satellite beam activation and energy, imperfect CSI, counterfactual credit assignment, fractional EE and simulation design. Research stopped after each requested topic had primary support or an explicit evidence limit; no comparable field measurement of C3-S-style evacuation or closed-loop C3-S outcome was found in the supplied evidence.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND3-CONSOLIDATION-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:32:| H19. Additive C3, set coordination and learned coordination are equivalent | [c3s_policy.py:230](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-screen/c3s_policy.py:230) | Separate proposal learning, unilateral search and joint consolidation; compare equal-information nominal S0 and learned S3. | P/M/T: singleton evacuation aliases and simulator access can be mislabelled as coordination/learning. | FIX | R1/R2, RT, C |
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND3-CONSOLIDATION-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:106:29. **C3.** A set-level consolidation coordinator operates on complete proposals, scores whole configurations with the same system objective/QoS terms, and commits atomically. BASE is always present and wins ties. Include unilateral proposals and genuine multi-user evacuations; count actual changed users, not catalogue labels. S0 uses deployable nominal physics; learned S3 must additionally beat matched S0.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND3-CONSOLIDATION-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:134:21. **System externality:** focal +1 bit, nonfocal −10 bits, ΔE=0 gives immediate teacher surplus −9, not +1; a two-user evacuation must be distinguishable from singleton aliases.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND3-CONSOLIDATION-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:173:- Run **S0** with deployable nominal information, fixed top-two per-user proposals and the same frozen evacuation decoder. Also run NULL, random-feasible and nominal-greedy controls. Oracle-selected profiles must never become S0 inputs.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-variants-chatgpt-package-20260908/OUTSIDE-ROUND4-CHATGPT-DEEP-RESEARCH-LITERATURE-REVIEW-2026-09-08.md:37:Implication for V-H: retain the exact rule and describe it as a three-decision coordinator override cooldown. File 01 explicitly says “BASE 可移動它且不重設鎖.” It can inhibit repeated coordinator moves, but cannot guarantee ping-pong suppression: BASE may reverse an override at the next decision. Excluding an entire evacuation when a member is locked also changes the available group moves. Three steps is a fixed coarse probe of intervention persistence; the cited literature supplies no universal timer of that length.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-c3s-variants-chatgpt-package-20260908/OUTSIDE-ROUND4-CHATGPT-DEEP-RESEARCH-LITERATURE-REVIEW-2026-09-08.md:72:The two catalogs do not isolate coalition causality. File 01, “Lite catalog” and the V-J/V-U rows, retains singleton origins in evacuations; those can duplicate unilateral moves. Evacuation destinations are unrestricted by Q12 top-2, whereas V-U has at most one alternative per user. Thus their differences combine group-move availability with proposal coverage. S0-J versus S0-U is not a pure estimate of joint interaction value, and V-U is not a replication of the full unilateral S0 catalog. The explicit caveats in 01 are correct and should survive paper compression.
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND1-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:48:**Mechanism:** adding a user below an existing beam maximum adds no PA or circuit power; removing the maximum user can reduce power abruptly; removing the last user deletes the beam’s entire draw. These are powerful association incentives. Bandwidth sharing supplies a countervailing cost, so consolidation is not automatically beneficial. **Exploiters:** all, especially C3-S’s evacuation catalog and joint oracles. **Magnitude:** at 0.825 W, PA plus circuit draw is **6.26590 W/beam**. Half an equivalent beam is **3.13295 W**, close to the reported 3.226 W saving. But “0.50 fewer beams” is an inference, not a recorded count. **Status:** DECLARED equations. **Handle: DECLARE and SENSITIVITY; resolve B02 before hardware interpretation.** [link_budget.py:442](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/link_budget.py:442), [EVIDENCE-02:129](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-physics/EVIDENCE-02-HARNESS-AUDIT-OPUS.md:129)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND1-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:51:**Mechanism:** an empty beam costs zero; an emptied satellite contributes zero. There is no retained PA bias, idle payload draw, minimum on-time or wake-up transient. The model therefore grants immediately realizable savings whenever resources become empty. Real savings depend on what can actually be powered down and for how long. **Exploiters:** all; evacuation search directly targets this discontinuity. **Magnitude:** potentially large for absolute EE and its energy-saving component. For fixed trajectories, adding a common **total** floor of 40/100/400 W reduces the reported FULL contrast to approximately 2.712/2.527/2.108%; an arbitrarily large common floor leaves the +1.6092% bits contrast. These are sensitivities, not hardware estimates. Four candidate slots per user do not establish four physical satellites. **Status:** partial boundary DECLARED; instant switching follows from the equations. **Handle: SENSITIVITY and explicit hardware boundary.** [link_budget.py:527](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/link_budget.py:527), [EVIDENCE-01:138](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-astra-physics/EVIDENCE-01-REDTEAM-OPUS.md:138)
.scratch/multi-catfish-v023-controller-handoff-20260907/ADJUDICATION-PHYSICS-EE-ROUND1-CODEX-GPT6-ASTRA-ULTRA-2026-09-08.md:91:**Mechanism:** interference includes every active co-colour beam in the simulated population, using beam-maximum RF power. Other colours are perfectly orthogonal; the serving beam is excluded; same-satellite beams receive full terminal gain because they arrive from the same direction. There is no external traffic field, imperfect orthogonality or independently scheduled beam activity. **Exploiters:** all, especially coordinated beam evacuation and colour-aware moves. **Magnitude:** both pooled EE and the contrast are sensitive to the interference field. An older probe found approximately 97.9% intra-satellite interference, but that is not the current panel’s decomposition. Removing a beam can therefore yield both PA savings and nonfocal rate gains. **Status:** DECLARED. **Handle: DECLARE scope; SENSITIVITY to scheduling and an independently specified background field.** [interference.py:277](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/interference.py:277), [interference.py:349](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/src/mcrl/env/interference.py:349), [LINK-BUDGET-NOTES.md:227](/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover-e1/docs/LINK-BUDGET-NOTES.md:227)
